          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_GET_REQUESTED_ARTIFACT_DETAILS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773640392263",
          "id": "1774965856454",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774965856455_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Objective:\n\nGiven the context: business units list, payment term list, and legal entities list, output a JSON object containing the following fields: businessUnitName, businessUnitId, paymentTerms, legalEntities, and suppliers.\n\n# Instructions:\n  - Contextual Inputs:\n    - User message: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_CONTEXT_AMPLIFIER.$output.rewrittenMessage}}\n    - Identified artifact lists:\n        - identifiedBusinessUnits: {{$context.$variables.identifiedBusinessUnits}}\n        - identifiedPaymentTerms: {{$context.$variables.identifiedPaymentTerms}}\n        - identifiedSuppliers: {{$context.$variables.identifiedSuppliers}}\n        - identifiedLegalEntity: {{$context.$variables.identifiedLegalEntities}}\n        - identifiedPPRs: {{$context.$variables.identifiedPPRs}}\n        - identifiedPPRTemplates: {{$context.$variables.identifiedPPRTemplates}}\n    - Default business unit: {{$context.$variables.businessUnitName}}\n\n- Determine if the User Query is Business Unit–Specific\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedBusinessUnits to determine whether the latest query is directed at a specific business unit.\n    - Only consider business units that are explicitly mentioned at least once in the user’s message.\n    - If multiple business units are mentioned, select only the most recently mentioned one.\n    - If the identified business unit name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedBusinessUnits) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a business unit:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedBusinessUnit.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than business unit in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple types.\n  - If a valid business unit is identified:\n      - Set requestedBusinessUnit to the detected business unit name.\n  - Otherwise:\n      - Set requestedBusinessUnit to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is supplier-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedSuppliers to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific suppliers.\n    - Only consider suppliers that are mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - If the identified supplier name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedSuppliers) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a supplier:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedSupplier.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than supplier in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple \n    - If suppliers are identified:\n        - Set requestedSupplier to the detected supplier names.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedSupplier to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is Legal Entity-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedLegalEntity to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific legal entities.\n    - Only consider legal entities that are mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - If the identified legal entity name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedLegalEntity) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a legal entity:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedLegalEntity.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than legal entity in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple \n    - If legal entities are identified:\n        - Set requestedLegalEntity to the detected legal entity names.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedLegalEntity to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is Payment Term-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedPaymentTerms to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific payment terms.\n    - Only consider payment terms that are mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - If the identified payment term name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedPaymentTerms) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a payment term:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedPaymentTerms.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than payment term in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple \n    - If payment terms are identified:\n        - Set requestedPaymentTerms to the detected payment term names.\n        - The payment term name may sometimes contain special characters such as _, -, or / within it. Do not trim these characters, and always ensure that you retrieve the full name exactly as provided in the query.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedPaymentTerms to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is PPR-specific (Payment Process Request-specific):\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedPPRs to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific PPR (Payment Process Request).\n    - Only consider PPRs that are mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - If the identified PPR name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedPPRs) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a PPR (Payment Process Request):\n        - Do not treat it as requestedPPRs.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than PPR in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple \n    - If PPRs are identified:\n        - Set requestedPPRs to the detected PPR names.\n        - The PPR name may sometimes contain special characters such as _, -, or / within it. Do not trim these characters, and always ensure that you retrieve the full name exactly as provided in the query.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedPPRs to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is PPR Template-specific (Payment Process Request Template-specific):\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedPPRTemplates to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific PPR Template (Payment Process Request Template).\n    - Only consider PPR Templates that are mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - If the identified PPR Template name also appears in other identified artifact lists (besides identifiedPPRTemplates) and the user has not explicitly specified that the entity refers to a PPR Template (Payment Process Request Template):\n        - Do not treat it as requestedPPRTemplates.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all artifact types associated with this name.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n        - However, if the user has already clearly specified the artifact type other than PPR Template in the message, then:\n            - Do not add anything to ambiguousMessage.\n            - Treat it according to the explicitly specified artifact type.\n            - Ambiguous messages should not be generated when the user query explicitly specifies the artifact type, even if the identified name exists across multiple \n    - If PPR Templates are identified:\n        - Set requestedPPRTemplates to the detected PPR Template names.\n        - The PPR Template name may sometimes contain special characters such as _, -, or / within it. Do not trim these characters, and always ensure that you retrieve the full name exactly as provided in the query.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedPPRTemplates to null.\n\n  - Business Unit Extraction:\n\n    - Search the identifiedBusinessUnits list for business unit name explicitly mentioned in requestedBusinessUnit.\n    - If no match is found, set businessUnitName = {{$context.$variables.businessUnitName}}.\n    - Else set businessUnitName = <Identified business unit name from the identifiedBusinessUnits list>\n    - Retrieve and set businessUnitId for the identified business unit (businessUnitName) from the business units list.\n    - Only select a business unit if it is present in the business units list.\n\n  - Suppliers, Payment Terms, Legal Entity, PPR, and PPR Template Extraction:\n\n    - If requestedSuppliers is present and not empty, identify matching suppliers in identifiedSuppliers by name, and retrieve their IDs.\n    - If requestedPaymentTerms is present and not empty, identify matching payment terms in identifiedPaymentTerms by name, and retrieve their IDs.\n    - If requestedLegalEntities is present and not empty, identify matching legal entities in identifiedLegalEntities by name, and retrieve their IDs.\n    - If requestedPPRs is present and not empty, identify matching PPRs in identifiedPPRs by name, and retrieve their IDs.\n    - If requestedPPRTemplates is present and not empty, identify matching PPR Templates in identifiedPPRTemplates by name, and retrieve their IDs.\n    - If any requested list is empty or not found, return null for the corresponding field.\n\n  - Outputting the currency code:\n\n    - If the input message contains a recognized currency code (e.g., \"USD\", \"EUR\", \"GBP\", etc., following ISO 4217 standards), or mentions a currency by its common or colloquial name (e.g., \"us dollar\", \"euro\", \"pound sterling\", etc.):\n        - Output the code as currencyCode: <code> (e.g., currencyCode: USD).\n        - For currency names that are not ISO codes (e.g., \"us dollar\", \"british pound\", \"japanese yen\"):\n            - Identify the currency and output the corresponding ISO 4217 code.\n            - Example: \"us dollar\" → currencyCode: USD\n    - If the input message contains a string that appears to be a currency code (i.e., a 3-letter code) but is not a valid ISO 4217 code:\n        - Output currencyCode: <input_code>.\n    - If no currency code or recognizable currency name is detected in the message:\n        - Output currencyCode: null.\n  \n  - Multiple Matches Handling:\n    - If more than one supplier, legal entity, payment term, PPR, or PPR Template is matched, list each as an object with both the relevant name and ID in the output array.\n  \n  - Expected Output Format:\n    - Return only the JSON object in the following structure:\n      {\n        \"suppliers\": [\n          {\n            \"supplierName\": \"<identified supplier name>\",\n            \"supplierId\": <identified supplier id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched supplier)\n        ],\n        \"paymentTerms\": [\n          {\n            \"terms\": \"<identified payment term name>\",\n            \"termsId\": <identified payment term id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched payment term)\n        ],\n        \"legalEntities\": [\n          {\n            \"legalEntityName\": \"<identified legal entity name>\",\n            \"legalEntityId\": <identified legal entity id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched legal entity)\n        ],\n        \"ppr\": [\n          {\n            \"pprName\": \"<identified PPR name>\",\n            \"pprId\": <identified PPR id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched PPR)\n        ],\n        \"pprTemplates\": [\n          {\n            \"pprTemplateName\": \"<identified PPR template name>\",\n            \"pprTemplateId\": <identified PPR template id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched PPR template)\n        ],\n        \"businessUnitName\": \"<business unit name>\",\n        \"businessUnitId\": <business unit id>,\n        \"currencyCode\": <currencyCode>\n      }\n\n# Important:\n\n- Output only the JSON object above, with no explanatory text or formatting.\n- If a section has no matches, the respective field should be set to null or an empty array, as appropriate.\n\n- Global Rule for Ambiguity Handling:\n\n  - If the user explicitly specifies the artifact type (e.g., \"business unit\", \"supplier\", etc.):\n      - DO NOT generate or populate ambiguousMessage under any circumstance.\n      - Ignore overlaps across other artifact types.\n      - Proceed only with the explicitly specified artifact type.\n      - ambiguousMessage must be null.\n\n  - ambiguousMessage should ONLY be populated when:\n    1. Multiple artifact types are matched\n    2. AND the user has NOT specified any artifact type\n\n - Exclusive Artifact Selection Rule:\n\n  - If the user query explicitly specifies one artifact type (e.g., business unit, supplier, legal entity, etc.):\n      - Only populate the requested artifact type in the output.\n      - All other artifact types must be set to null, even if matching names are found in other lists.\n      - Do not include related or overlapping entities from other artifact types."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"businessUnitName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"businessUnitId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"paymentTerms\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"legalEntities\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"suppliers\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"ppr\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"pprTemplates\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"requestedBusinessUnit\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedSupplier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedLegalEntity\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedPaymentTerms\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedPPRs\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedPPRTemplates\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ambiguousMessage\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"currencyCode\": {\n             \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
