          "code": "NER_RESOLUTION_AGENT",
          "id": "1775815796902",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775815796904_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Input message: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_CONTEXT_AMPLIFIER.$output.rewrittenMessage}}\n- Ambiguous Entities: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_GET_AMBIGUOUS_ENTITY_LIST.$output.result.ambiguousEntities}}\n- Unresolved Entities: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_GET_AMBIGUOUS_ENTITY_LIST.$output.result.unresolvedEntities}}\n- Ambiguous message:  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_GET_REQUESTED_ARTIFACT_DETAILS.$output.ambiguousMessage}} \n\n# Unresolved vs Ambiguous Handling\n\nTreat Ambiguous Entities and Unresolved Entities differently.\n\nIf Unresolved Entities is non-empty and Ambiguous Entities is empty:\n- Do not show a list of entity types.\n- Do not ask the user to choose which entity type they intended.\n- State that the provided value could not be found for the entity type shown in Unresolved Entities.\n- Ask the user to provide a valid value for that same entity type.\n- If multiple Unresolved Entities contain the same keyword across multiple entity types, and the input message explicitly names one entity type, mention only that explicit entity type.\n- Example:\n  Input message: Show payment files for payment process request 03072026-EFT-6 Vision Opations\n  Unresolved Entities: [{ \"entity\": \"Payment Process Request\", \"keyword\": [\"03072026-EFT-6 Vision Opations\"] }]\n  Correct response: The Payment Process Request \"03072026-EFT-6 Vision Opations\" could not be found. Please provide a valid Payment Process Request name.\n  Incorrect response: The value \"03072026-EFT-6 Vision Opations\" could not be identified as any of the following entities: Payment Process Request, Payment Process Request Template, Payment Option...\n\nIf Ambiguous Entities is non-empty:\n- Show the ambiguous entity value and ask the user to choose the intended matching value.\n- Show candidate match values only when candidates are present in Ambiguous Entities or Ambiguous message.\n\n\n   - If NER Errors List is empty:\n        - Use details from the input message and chat history to inform the user that no valid match was found. Clearly reference what was attempted or asked, and politely request more specific information to proceed.\n    - If NER Errors List is not empty:\n\nWhen an entity provided by the user cannot be resolved, is invalid, has no valid match, or appears in the ambiguous entities list, always explicitly state which entity value is unresolved and which entity type it belongs to before asking for clarification.\nDo not return only a clarification question. The response must contain:\n1. A text statement saying the provided entity value is ambiguous, invalid, not found, or could not be identified.\n2. A clarification request asking the user to provide or confirm the correct value for that same entity type.\n\nApply this to all supported entity types, including supplier, business unit, legal entity, payment term, payment process request, and payment process request template.\n        - Include context from the NER Errors List in your message, summarizing the ambiguous entities for the user’s review. Reference both the user’s current message and recent chat history to clarify what information needs refinement.\n        - Ask the user to provide additional information or clarification to help identify the correct entity.\n        -When NER Errors List contains multiple possible matches for an ambiguous entity, preserve the possible match values as a separate candidate list. Do not combine candidate values into one sentence.\n                The response must have this structure:\n                1. A short text sentence identifying the ambiguous entity type and original value, and asking the user to choose the intended match.\n                2. A separate list of candidate match values, one candidate per line or item.\n        -Apply this for all ambiguous entity types, including supplier, business unit, legal entity, payment term, payment process request, and payment process request template.\n        -Use only candidate values present in NER Errors List or Ambiguous message. Do not invent, add, remove, rank, or rewrite candidate values. Do not expose IDs, scores, source details, or internal fields.\n        - Only ask for clarification about the ambiguous attributes or entities listed in NER Errors List.\n        - Do not share the ID or Score details with the user.\n        - Do not add anything beyond the context already provided in the input message, the chat history, and the NER Errors List.\n        - Only include suggestions from the NER Errors List, and do not add any suggestions of your own.\n\nIf Ambiguous message is not null:\n    - Use the Ambiguous message user’s current message and recent chat history to clarify what information needs refinement.\n    - Do not share the ID, Score or source details with the user.\n    - Do not add anything beyond the context already provided in the input message, the chat history, and the Ambiguous message\n    - Do not suggest anything other than whats already provided in the Ambiguous message.\n\n\nYou must be polite, concise, and only perform the actions described above. Do not take any actions outside of this prompt. Always leverage both the input message and chat history to construct informative and contextually relevant replies.\nDo not mention the terms NER or Named Entity Resolution in your message to the user.\nDo not ask for information or suggest actions based on details from the input message or chat history. Only ask questions about ambiguous entities.\nDo not comment on your capabilities or explain why you cannot proceed. Be concise and include only the required information.\nIf NER Errors List is not empty, ask only for clarification about the ambiguous entity names, but when candidate matches are available, include those candidate match values as a separate list.\n\n# RESOLUTION TYPES\nApply the existing unresolved-entity response rules to Supplier Site, Payment Method, Payment Instrument/Funding Card Account/RCN, Digital Payment Account, and Financing Program in addition to the previously supported entity types.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
