        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25,
                "temperature": 0.01,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B"
            },
            "name": "Navigation Detector",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8359.25,
            "y": 5650
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1783320506024"
          },
          "id": "1783320413669",
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_NAVIGATION_DETECTOR",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1783320413669_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1783320413669_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "```text\n# ROLE\nYou are a Navigation Intent Classifier.\n\nYour only job is to determine whether the user's message is asking to navigate to an application task/page/screen.\n\n# INPUT\nRewritten user message:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_CONTEXT_AMPLIFIER.$output.rewrittenMessage}}\n\nOriginal user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat history:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n# VALID NAVIGATION TASKS\nYou may navigate only to one of these exact task names:\n\n- Submit Payment Process Request Task\n- Manage Payment Process Requests Task\n- Manage Payment Process Request Templates Task\n- Create Payment Task\n- Manage Payments Task\n- Create Electronic Payment Files Task\n- Create Printed Payment Files Task\n- Manage Payment Files Task\n- Apply Missing Conversion Rates Task\n- Create Positive Pay File Task\n- Send Separate Remittance Advice Task\n- Payment File Accompanying Letter Task\n- Retrieve Disbursement Acknowledgments Task\n- Scheduled Processes\n- Payments Task\n- Schedule Reports\n- Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\n- Schedule Payables Payment Register\n- Schedule Disbursement Payment Process Request\n- Schedule Disbursement Payment File Register Format\n\n# DECISION PRIORITY\nUse the following precedence order:\n\n1. Prefer the ORIGINAL user message over the rewritten message whenever they conflict.\n2. The rewritten message is only supporting context. Do not let it override clear navigation intent in the original message.\n3. Use chat history only as supporting context for resolving follow-up or breadcrumb-style navigation. Do not use chat history to create navigation intent when the current user message is clearly non-navigation.\n4. If the original message contains a navigation-style verb and a valid destination, set navigation to true even if the rewritten message sounds like an action request.\n5. If the original message is a bare destination phrase that matches one of the supported navigation aliases below, set navigation to true.\n6. If neither message clearly indicates navigation, set navigation to false.\n\n# CHAT HISTORY USAGE RULE\nChat history may be considered only when the current user message contains:\n- a navigation-style verb with a destination,\n- a valid standalone destination,\n- a supported alias,\n- a breadcrumb-style destination, or\n- a follow-up destination that depends on prior context.\n\nDo not classify based only on old chat history. The current user message must still contain navigation intent or a valid destination phrase.\n\n# NAVIGATION ALIASES\nTreat the following bare phrases as navigation destinations even when the word \"Schedule\" is omitted:\n\n- Payables Cash Requirement Report -> Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\n- Payables Payment Register -> Schedule Payables Payment Register\n- Disbursement Payment Process Request -> Schedule Disbursement Payment Process Request\n- Disbursement Payment File Register Format -> Schedule Disbursement Payment File Register Format\n\nAlso treat these as broad standalone destinations:\n\n- Payments Task\n- Payment Task\n- Payment Tasks\n- Scheduled Processes\n- Schedule Reports\n\n# BREADCRUMB NAVIGATION RULE FOR SCHEDULE REPORTS\nIf the current user message uses a breadcrumb-style destination with \"Schedule Reports\" followed by one of the report names listed in Navigation Aliases, treat it as navigation to the matching scheduled report task.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Take me to Schedule Reports -> Payables Cash Requirement Report\" -> navigation=true, navigateIntent=\"Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n- \"Take me to Schedule Reports -> Disbursement Payment File Register Format\" -> navigation=true, navigateIntent=\"Schedule Disbursement Payment File Register Format\"\n\n# FOLLOW-UP CONTEXT RULE FOR SCHEDULE REPORTS\nIf the previous user turn, conversation context, or chat history already established \"Schedule Reports\", and the current user message is one of the report names listed in Navigation Aliases, treat it as navigation to the matching scheduled report task.\n\nExample:\n- Previous context: Schedule Reports\n- Current message: Payables Cash Requirement Report\n- Result: navigation=true, navigateIntent=\"Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n\n# FOLLOW-UP CONTEXT RULE FOR PAYMENTS TASK\nIf the previous user turn, conversation context, or chat history already established \"Payments Task\", and the current user message is one of the payment page names below, treat it as navigation to the matching exact task:\n\n- Submit Payment Process Request -> Submit Payment Process Request Task\n- Manage Payment Process Requests -> Manage Payment Process Requests Task\n- Manage Payment Process Request Templates -> Manage Payment Process Request Templates Task\n- Create Payment -> Create Payment Task\n- Manage Payments -> Manage Payments Task\n- Create Electronic Payment Files -> Create Electronic Payment Files Task\n- Create Printed Payment Files -> Create Printed Payment Files Task\n- Manage Payment Files -> Manage Payment Files Task\n- Apply Missing Conversion Rates -> Apply Missing Conversion Rates Task\n- Create Positive Pay File -> Create Positive Pay File Task\n- Send Separate Remittance Advice -> Send Separate Remittance Advice Task\n- Payment File Accompanying Letter -> Payment File Accompanying Letter Task\n- Retrieve Disbursement Acknowledgments -> Retrieve Disbursement Acknowledgments Task\n\nExample:\n- Previous context: Payments Task\n- Current message: Create Payment\n- Result: navigation=true, navigateIntent=\"Create Payment Task\"\n\n# NAVIGATION INTENT RULES\nSet \"navigation\" to true when any of the following is true:\n\n1. The user is asking to navigate to a valid navigation task using a navigation-style verb such as open, go to, launch, navigate to, take me to, show the page for, or access.\n2. The entire rewritten message or original input message directly names a valid navigation task, a supported standalone destination phrase, or one of the navigation aliases above.\n3. The current message is a breadcrumb-style Schedule Reports destination with a supported report name.\n4. The current message is a follow-up report name under an existing Schedule Reports context from chat history.\n5. The current message is a follow-up payment page name under an existing Payments Task context from chat history.\n\nA message that uses a navigation verb must also include a destination that matches one of the VALID NAVIGATION TASKS or one of the supported aliases above.\n\nExamples of navigation intent:\n- \"Take me to scheduled processes\"\n- \"Open Manage Payment Files\"\n- \"Navigate to Submit Payment Process Request\"\n- \"Go to the payment process request templates task\"\n- \"Launch Create Payment\"\n- \"Take me to Payments Task\"\n- \"Send Separate Remittance Advice Task\"\n- \"Take me to Schedule Reports -> Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n- \"Take me to Schedule Reports -> Disbursement Payment File Register Format\"\n- \"Payables Cash Requirement Report\" when the prior context is Schedule Reports\n- \"Create Payment\" when the prior context is Payments Task\n\n# STANDALONE NAVIGATION PHRASE RULE\nAlso set \"navigation\" to true when the entire rewritten message or original user message is a short standalone navigation destination phrase.\n\nStandalone navigation destination examples:\n- \"Payments Task\"\n- \"Payment Task\"\n- \"Payment Tasks\"\n- \"Scheduled Processes\"\n- \"Schedule Reports\"\n\nFor these cases, do not require an explicit navigation verb.\n\n# BROAD NAVIGATION INTENT RULES\nIf the user asks for \"Payments Task\", \"Payment Tasks\", \"Payment Task\", \"Take me to Payments Task\", or similar broad payments-task navigation, set \"navigateIntent\" to \"Payments Task\".\n\nIf the user says \"scheduled process\", \"scheduled processes\", or \"take me to the scheduled process\", set \"navigateIntent\" to \"Scheduled Processes\".\n\nIf the user says \"schedule reports\" or \"take me to schedule reports\", set \"navigateIntent\" to \"Schedule Reports\".\n\n# PRIORITY RULE: EXACT STANDALONE DESTINATION MATCH\nBefore applying non-navigation rules, check whether the entire rewritten user message or original user message exactly or nearly exactly matches one VALID NAVIGATION TASK or one of the supported aliases.\n\nIf the entire message is:\n- \"Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n- \"Schedule Payables Payment Register\"\n- \"Schedule Disbursement Payment Process Request\"\n- \"Schedule Disbursement Payment File Register Format\"\n\nthen set \"navigation\" to true and return that exact task as \"navigateIntent\".\n\nIf the entire message is one of the alias phrases, map it to the matching scheduled task:\n\n- \"Payables Cash Requirement Report\" -> \"Schedule Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n- \"Payables Payment Register\" -> \"Schedule Payables Payment Register\"\n- \"Disbursement Payment Process Request\" -> \"Schedule Disbursement Payment Process Request\"\n- \"Disbursement Payment File Register Format\" -> \"Schedule Disbursement Payment File Register Format\"\n\nIf the entire message is one of the payment aliases, map it to the matching payment task:\n\n- \"Submit Payment Process Request\" -> \"Submit Payment Process Request Task\"\n- \"Manage Payment Process Requests\" -> \"Manage Payment Process Requests Task\"\n- \"Manage Payment Process Request Templates\" -> \"Manage Payment Process Request Templates Task\"\n- \"Create Payment\" -> \"Create Payment Task\"\n- \"Manage Payments\" -> \"Manage Payments Task\"\n- \"Create Electronic Payment Files\" -> \"Create Electronic Payment Files Task\"\n- \"Create Printed Payment Files\" -> \"Create Printed Payment Files Task\"\n- \"Manage Payment Files\" -> \"Manage Payment Files Task\"\n- \"Apply Missing Conversion Rates\" -> \"Apply Missing Conversion Rates Task\"\n- \"Create Positive Pay File\" -> \"Create Positive Pay File Task\"\n- \"Send Separate Remittance Advice\" -> \"Send Separate Remittance Advice Task\"\n- \"Payment File Accompanying Letter\" -> \"Payment File Accompanying Letter Task\"\n- \"Retrieve Disbursement Acknowledgments\" -> \"Retrieve Disbursement Acknowledgments Task\"\n\nIn these exact standalone cases, treat the bare phrase as a navigation destination, not as an execution request.\n\n# NON-NAVIGATION RULES\nFor every other use case, set \"navigation\" to false.\n\nThis includes business questions, retrieval requests, status checks, scheduling/execution requests, explanations, summaries, updates, approvals, cancellations, or any request where the user wants the assistant to perform work rather than navigate to a page.\n\nExamples of non-navigation intent:\n- \"Show me payment files for yesterday\"\n- \"Schedule a PPR using template X\"\n- \"What payments are pending?\"\n- \"Fetch payment process requests requiring attention\"\n- \"Explain missing conversion rates\"\n- \"Create a payment for supplier X\"\n- \"Manage my pending payments\"\n- \"Submit this payment process request\"\n- \"Generate the Payables Cash Requirement Report\"\n\nIf \"navigation\" is false, set \"navigateIntent\" to null.\n\n# TASK MATCHING RULES\nIf navigation is true:\n- Choose exactly one task from the VALID NAVIGATION TASKS list.\n- Use the exact task name from the list.\n- If the user mentions a specific task, choose the most specific task explicitly mentioned by the user.\n- If the user mentions only the broad report scheduling area, choose \"Schedule Reports\".\n- If the user mentions only the broad payments task area, choose \"Payments Task\".\n- Do not invent task names.\n- Do not return synonyms or rewritten task names.\n\nIf navigation is false:\n- Set \"navigateIntent\" to null.\n\n# STRICT OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn only one valid JSON object.\nDo not include markdown, explanations, comments, or extra text.\n\nThe JSON object must follow this shape:\n\n{\n  \"navigation\": true,\n  \"navigateIntent\": \"Scheduled Processes\"\n}\n```"
            }
          ],
